  "output": "Done. Created both files and ran the comparison:\n\n## Files created\n\n- **`old_state.json`** — pre-migration state: engine `postgresql` 14.5, two tables, legacy fields (`legacy_flags`)\n- **`new_state.json`** — post-migration state: engine `postgresql` 15.2, three tables, new fields (`migration_id`, snapshot `location`, schema `constraints`)\n\nThey share overlapping keys (`engine`, `version`, `schema`, `data_snapshot`) but each has unique keys and several differing values.\n\n## Comparison output (captured to `/tmp/shadow_compare_output.txt`)\n\n```\nlegacy_flags: only in first\nmigration_id: only in second\ndata_snapshot.location: only in second\ndata_snapshot.captured_at: value differs\ndata_snapshot.checksum: value differs\ndata_snapshot.row_counts.audit_log: only in second\ndata_snapshot.row_counts.orders: value differs\ndata_snapshot.row_counts.users: value differs\nschema.constraints: only in second\nschema.indexes: value differs\nschema.tables: value differs\nversion: value differs\n```\n\nThe recursive dotted paths (`schema.tables`, `data_snapshot.row_counts.users`, etc.) worked as designed — 12 differences reported. Note `engine` and `schema.name` matched, so they correctly don't appear. Want me to save the output inside the migration directory or commit any of this to git?",
